  "custom_logic_notes": "Core logic is multi-indicator divergence detection: finds peaks/troughs in price and each indicator (RSI, MACD, Stochastic) over BarsToCheck bars, requires MinBarsDistance between extrema. Bullish divergence = price makes lower low while indicator makes higher low. Bearish divergence = price makes higher high while indicator makes lower high. Requires MinConfirmations (1-3) of the 3 indicators to agree. Divergence strength must exceed MinDivergenceStrength (0-1). Optional trend filter requires price above MA for longs, below MA for shorts. Optional volume filter requires current volume > 1.2x 10-bar average. Peak/trough detection has a secondary averaging filter that rejects peaks not sufficiently above local average. Bid/Ask globals are incorrectly assigned as SYMBOL_ASK/SYMBOL_BID constants instead of actual prices — bug in original code.",
