    "Trade\\Trade.mqh"
  ],
  "estimated_difficulty": "medium",
  "backtest_data_needs": "M1",
  "python_conversion_notes": "Divergence detection (FindPeaksAndTroughs) requires porting the peak/trough identification algorithm with MinBarsDistance lookback and the secondary averaging filter. The divergence strength formula must be replicated exactly. All three indicator divergence checks follow the same pattern — can be refactored into a single generic function. Note the original code has a bug on lines 49-50 where Ask/Bid are set to enum constants instead of SymbolInfoDouble calls — the Python version should use proper price fetching. SL/TP use Point() directly without 5-digit adjustment, so the Python version should use the raw point value. Position counting uses PositionsTotal with magic number filter. Volume handle uses VOLUME_TICK which may not map directly to all Python data sources.",
